---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ProductGrid from '../../components/ProductGrid.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/quote/QuoteForm.tsx';
import { serviceSchema } from '../../lib/schema/service';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema/faqPage';
import { getAllProducts } from '../../data/catalog/shopify';
import '../../styles/quote-form.css';

const allProducts = await getAllProducts();
const products = allProducts.filter((p) => p.tags.includes('centerpiece')).slice(0, 9);

const faqs = (await getCollection('faq'))
  .filter((f) => f.data.pages.includes('centerpieces'))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .map((f) => ({ question: f.data.question, body: f.body.trim() }));

const schemas = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Balloon centerpieces',
    description:
      'Custom balloon centerpieces and table arrangements, delivered and placed for events in London Ontario.',
    startingPrice: 39,
    url: '/services/centerpieces',
  }),
];
if (faqs.length > 0) {
  schemas.push(faqPageSchema(faqs.map((f) => ({ question: f.question, answer: f.body }))));
}
---

<BaseLayout
  topic="Balloon Centerpieces"
  description="Balloon centerpieces for events in London Ontario. Built to your palette, sized so guests can see across the table, delivered and placed. From $39 per table."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services' },
    { name: 'Centerpieces', url: '/services/centerpieces' },
  ]}
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Install type"
    headline="Balloon centerpieces in London, Ontario"
    subhead="Table pieces built to your palette and sized so guests can still see each other across the table. Delivered and placed."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/quote', label: 'Start a quote' }}
    secondaryCta={{ href: '/portfolio', label: 'See centerpiece work' }}
    image="/images/categories/centerpieces.webp"
    imageAlt="Balloon centerpiece in soft tones"
    variant="page"
  />

  <section class="install-body section">
    <div class="container container-narrow prose">
      <p>
        Centerpieces are the piece guests spend the most time looking at, because they sit at eye level
        for however long people are at the table. They are also the easiest thing to get wrong, and
        almost always in the same way: too tall.
      </p>

      <h2>What balloon centerpieces cost</h2>
      <p>
        Simple table pieces start at $39. Standard centerpieces for a shower, birthday, or corporate
        lunch run $55 to $109. Larger statement pieces for head tables, gift tables, and dessert
        displays reach $139 and up. Because most events order several, we quote by the set rather than
        the piece, and the per-table number comes down as the count rises.
      </p>

      <h2>How many you actually need</h2>
      <p>
        One per guest table is the default, and for most events in London that lands between six and
        twelve. Before ordering that many, it is worth knowing that not every table needs the same
        thing. A common approach is a full piece on the head table, the gift table, and the cake or
        dessert table, then something smaller and lower on guest tables.
      </p>
      <p>
        Height is the detail that gets missed. Anything above about fourteen inches on a dining table
        blocks sightlines, and guests quietly move it themselves partway through the meal, which is the
        clearest sign a centerpiece was built wrong. We build guest table pieces low and wide, and save
        the tall ones for tables nobody sits at. For corporate events and galas with rounds seating ten,
        we usually recommend fewer, larger pieces rather than one on every table.
      </p>

      <h2>Delivered and placed, not dropped off</h2>
      <p>
        Centerpieces arrive built and get placed on the tables, so nobody on your side is assembling
        anything the morning of. If the venue is still setting linens when we arrive, we work around
        them or come back, and Brenda coordinates that timing directly. For events where the room turns
        over between a ceremony and a reception, we can place them during the turnover instead.
      </p>
      <p>
        Send your table count and layout and we will tell you where pieces actually earn their spot
        rather than quoting one for every surface. Quantity guidance is in the
        <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>. For taller freestanding pieces see
        <a href="/services/columns">balloon columns</a>, and for something running the length of a head
        table see <a href="/services/balloon-garlands">balloon garlands</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {products.length > 0 && (
    <section class="install-products section">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Shop the catalog</p>
          <h2>Centerpieces in the catalog</h2>
          <p class="lede">Pick a build as-is or use it as the base for a custom version.</p>
        </header>
        <ProductGrid products={products} columns={3} />
        <p class="section-link-wrap">
          <a class="section-link" href="https://shop.balloonia.events/collections/centerpieces-columns">View all centerpieces →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  {faqs.length > 0 && <FAQAccordion heading="Centerpiece questions" faqs={faqs} />}

  <section class="install-quote section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Custom build</p>
        <h2>Working out a table plan?</h2>
        <p class="lede">Send your table count, layout, and colours. Brenda quotes the set within 24 hours.</p>
      </header>
      <QuoteForm client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p { color: var(--color-ink-soft); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); line-height: var(--line-relaxed); }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .prose a { color: var(--color-accent-deep); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .section-head { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .install-quote { background: var(--color-paper-soft); }
  .section-link { color: var(--color-accent-deep); font-size: var(--font-size-sm); font-weight: 500; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .section-link-wrap { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
